title: GDT AA (Alter Adventurer) — score setting and its rejections
story: dungeo
description: |
  AA SCORE sets the player's total to an exact value so a test can start from a
  scored position without replaying a walkthrough. The score ledger (ADR-129) is
  append-only with unique ids and no setter, so AA carries the difference in one
  reserved entry (gdt.score.adjustment) and leaves earned entries intact.

  Covers the rejection paths as well as the happy path.
---

[GOAL: AA SCORE sets an exact total and rejects bad input]

> gdt
[OK: contains "GDT"]

# --- happy path: an exact total, from zero ---
> aa score 493
[OK: contains "493"]
> ex
[OK: contains "Returning"]
> score
[OK: contains "493 out of 616"]

# --- idempotent: setting again REPLACES the adjustment, never stacks ---
# A naive implementation that appended a second ledger entry would land on 986.
> gdt
[OK: contains "GDT"]
> aa score 493
[OK: contains "493"]
> ex
[OK: contains "Returning"]
> score
[OK: contains "493 out of 616"]

# --- a different value overwrites cleanly, downward included ---
> gdt
[OK: contains "GDT"]
> aa score 25
[OK: contains "25"]
> ex
[OK: contains "Returning"]
> score
[OK: contains "25 out of 616"]

# --- rejections: each names the problem and leaves the score untouched ---
> gdt
[OK: contains "GDT"]

# no attribute
> aa
[OK: contains "Usage"]

# unknown attribute
> aa bogus 5
[OK: contains "Unknown adventurer attribute"]

# attribute with no value
> aa score
[OK: contains "Usage"]

# not a number
> aa score twelve
[OK: contains "Not a non-negative integer"]

# negative
> aa score -5
[OK: contains "Not a non-negative integer"]

> ex
[OK: contains "Returning"]

# The rejected calls changed nothing — still the last successful value.
> score
[OK: contains "25 out of 616"]

[END GOAL]
